  "content": {
    "title": "Liverpool confirmed XI vs. PSG: Salah DROPPED, Frimpong starts",
    "text": "Arne Slot has left Mohamed Salah on the bench for Liverpool’s biggest game of the season so far, with Jeremie Frimpong one of those brought in against PSG. Liverpool vs. PSG: Team News Changes: 2 (IN: Frimpong, Mac Allister | OUT: Salah, Jones) Formation: 3-4-2-1 Average XI Age: 25.5 Liverpool go into a game many expect them to lose with two changes from their 4-0 defeat to Man City in the FA Cup.Report Ad Giorgi Mamardashvili is one of those retained, with the Georgian set to keep his place in goal for at least the rest of the month in Alisson‘s absence. He starts behind a back three of Joe Gomez, Ibrahima Konate and Virgil van Dijk. A switch to a 3-4-2-1 formation therefore sees Jeremie Frimpong and Milos Kerkez as wing-backs and a midfield of Ryan Gravenberch and Alexis Mac Allister. Dominik Szoboszlai and Florian Wirtz are tasked with supporting Hugo Ekitike up front. Report Ad Slot is able to call upon Alexander Isak for the first time in 2026 as the Swede takes a place on the bench. Liverpool: Mamardashvili; Gomez, Konate, Van Dijk; Frimpong, Gravenberch, Mac Allister, Kerkez; Szoboszlai, Wirtz; Ekitike Substitutes: Woodman, Misciur, Robertson, Jones, Nyoni, Gakpo, Chiesa, Ngumoha, Isak, Salah PSG: Safonov; Hakimi, Pacho, Marquinhos, Nuno Mendes; Joao Neves, Vitinha, Zaire-Emery; Doue, Kvaratskhelia, Dembele Substitutes: Chevalier, Marin, Beraldo, Zabarnyi, Hernandez, Mayulu, Lee, Mbaye, Fernandez, Ramos PSG vs. Liverpool: TV & Streaming Info Subscribe to This Is Anfield on YouTube Join over 370,000 subscribers to get the latest LFC videos to your feed How to Watch PSG vs. Liverpool in the UK PSG vs. Liverpool is being shown live on TNT Sports 1 in the UK, which is available to live stream with HBO Max here.Report Ad Live audio commentary of PSG vs. Liverpool and a full match replay and highlights will also be available on All Red Video here. This Is Anfield will also be providing live text commentary throughout on our website and full match reaction and analysis on the This Is Anfield app for iPhone and Android later. Download free here.",
